# Beat (week 1, Monday) — coffee with the parent in the Truth. cast.md § 3.1:
# "Morning conversations over coffee about how the meeting went"; "I was
# talking to Brother Phillips and he mentioned..."; questions that aren't
# really questions.
# TODO: authenticity check

Monday. {GameState.parent_word} is already at the kitchen table when you come down. The coffee's made. Yesterday's Lighthouse is still open to the study article, the answers underlined in two colors.
if GameState.attended_this_month() > 0:
	"There you are. Wasn't that a good meeting yesterday? That talk. I thought of you the whole time."
else:
	"There you are. We missed you yesterday. Brother Phillips asked after you." A sip of coffee. "I said you weren't feeling well. You weren't, were you?"
"I was talking to Brother Phillips after. He says you've been such a help in the car group." A pause for the coffee. "He notices, you know. They all notice."
- "It was a good talk."
	"It was, wasn't it?" {GameState.parent_word} squeezes your hand once and goes back to the article.
- "I don't really remember what it was about."
	[signal arg="STANDING:family:-1"]
	A small laugh that doesn't quite finish. "Well. You were tired. We'll look at it together tonight, maybe."
You rinse your cup. The article stays open on the table after you leave.
